  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given an array AAA containing NNN positive integers.\n\nCount the number of ordered pairs of **disjoint** non-empty subsequences (S1,S2)(S_1, S_2)(S1​,S2​) such that gcd⁡(S1)=mex(S2)\\gcd(S_1) = \\text{mex}(S_2)gcd(S1​)=mex(S2​).\n\nHere, the mex of a sequence of integers is the smallest **positive** integer that doesn't appear in it.\n\nPrint the answer modulo 998244353998244353998244353.\n\nNote that:\n\n\nA subsequence of AAA is a sequence obtained by taking any subset S⊆{1,2,…,N}S\\subseteq \\{1, 2, \\ldots, N\\}S⊆{1,2,…,N} and looking at the sequence of elements corresponding to SSS.\nTwo subsequences are considered different if they are obtained from different index sets, even if the elements in the resulting sequence are equal.\n\nThus, an array of length NNN has exactly 2N2^N2N subsequences (including the empty sequence).\nTwo subsequences are considered disjoint if their index sets do not intersect.\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of two lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the number of valid pairs of subsequences, modulo 998244353998244353998244353.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "1≤N≤2⋅1051 \\leq N \\leq 2\\cdot 10^51≤N≤2⋅105",
      "1≤Ai≤1061 \\leq A_i \\leq 10^61≤Ai​≤106",
      "The sum of NNN across all tests won't exceed 2⋅1052\\cdot 10^52⋅105.",
      "The sum of max⁡(A)\\max(A)max(A) across all tests won't exceed 10610^6106."
    ],
